{title:The Glowing Hand}
{key:}

I see a glowing hand suspended in mid air
Somehow held aloft and all alone
Surrounded by a slowly fading darkness
That tomorrows dawning will soon own

I search for an explanation
Something complex and worthy of thought
What if that hand is the sole survivor
Of a battle that our God once fought?

Perhaps the glowing hand in the sky
Pinches between its finger and thumb
A tiny hole in the fabric of existence
That threatens to consume everyone

Tomorrow night I shall return
To salute the glowing hand with a prayer
I will watch as my existence remains steadfast
Thankful that the glowing hand is still there
